3.2 Substantial Similarity & Anti-Evasion
A work shall be deemed a Derivative Work if it is substantially similar in structure, logic, expression, architecture, core algorithms, data models, interfaces, system behavior, prompt patterns, or input-output sequences, regardless of the programming language, framework, or implementation method used.

Minor or superficial modifications (including renaming, formatting, reorganization, modularization, or reimplementation of substantially similar functionality) do not exclude a work from this definition. Attempts to avoid the application of this License through such means shall not prevent its application.

3.3 Commercial Use & Revenue Model
Safe Harbor: If your annual Gross Revenue from the product or service is less than $1,000 USD, no fee is required, provided you fully comply with the attribution requirements in Section 3.1.

Default Royalty: Upon exceeding the Safe Harbor threshold, a default royalty of 1% of Gross Revenue attributable to the Work applies.  

Revenue is considered attributable where the Work constitutes a core functional component, a significant technical element, or a material contributor to user-facing value. Where the contribution is not self-evident, a reasonable allocation shall be determined in good faith.

Use of the Work in a commercial context without a separately negotiated agreement constitutes acceptance of these default terms. You must maintain accurate records sufficient to demonstrate compliance and provide a summary or signed declaration upon reasonable written request from the Licensor.

